# Docker build context exclusion. The Rust Dockerfile already copies
# exactly what it needs (Cargo.toml + crates/), but having an
# explicit `.dockerignore` keeps `docker build` fast and prevents
# accidentally baking in build artifacts, the local SQLite DB, etc.
#
# Patterns overlap with `.gitignore`; this file is read by `docker
# build` only and has no effect on git itself.

# Local build artifacts
target/
**/target/
build/
dist/

# Local data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
data/
.cache/

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Test artifacts
**/tests/.tmp/
coverage/
*.profraw

# The Rust source itself is included — only the build outputs are
# excluded. We deliberately keep:
#   * Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock
#   * crates/ (the entire workspace)
#   * Dockerfile.rust
#   * .dockerignore
